
Consolidated below. Two things to sign off inside it: a small addition to reply handling that the vertical layout makes necessary (§4, G.3b), and the changelog line recording the echo threshold as *deliberately dropped* rather than omitted (§7).

On the vertical rendering — your call, and implemented as asked. I'll note that my "reads as a menu" objection was never about bullets per se but about *addressable* entries. Bullets are fine; indices are not. G.3b closes that gap so the layout change costs nothing.

