# Goal — Consolidated Amendments (this review)

## §0 Scope

Amends four areas: slot partition, objective determination, unresolved-slot rendering, Type 2 scaffolding. Section numbers are provisional and map by content, not by number, if the live spec differs.

Self-contained: no clause here depends on any other engine, prompt, or review session. Where earlier drafts justified a rule by reference to a downstream consumer, the rule is restated below in terms of *any* reader of the contract, including a human.

---

## §1 Slot partition

```
D.8  SLOT CLASSES

  Every contract slot belongs to exactly one class.

  DEFINITION SLOTS — describe what the goal is. May remain
    unresolved after discovery; if so they render "not established"
    and are listed in open:.

      objective · audience · environment · form

  REQUIREMENT SLOTS — describe constraints on, or tests of, the
    goal. If unaddressed they render "none stated", which is
    terminal. They never enter open:.

      exclusions · invalidation · success · horizon · register · …

  The definition class is closed at four. open: is bounded by the
  size of this class; adding a fifth definition slot widens that
  bound and requires re-review of D.11.

  No slot is ever omitted from the contract. An absent field and an
  unconsidered field are indistinguishable to a reader.
```

**Reviewer dependency:** the four definition slots must be confirmed against live spec naming. If the live spec has a fifth, the `open:` bound becomes five and §3 needs re-reading.

---

## §2 Determination

```
D.9  DETERMINATION

  A slot is determined where the input fixes its value under a
  single reading. Determined slots are populated verbatim or by
  minimal transcription. Undetermined slots are never populated by
  inference, default, or convention.

D.9a  OBJECTIVE FROM ARTEFACT

  Objective MAY be populated as the existence or completion of a
  named artefact, where a completion test is available from the
  input alone.

  Constraint: the populated value MUST introduce no noun absent
  from the input. If stating the end state requires a noun the
  user did not supply, objective is not determined.

  Undetermined → "not established" → open:.

  Where objective opens because the artefact name lacks a subject,
  the Type 2 question asks for that subject. It does not ask for a
  purpose behind the artefact.

  Worked:
    "summarize this report"
      → a summary of the attached report exists          determined
    "write an SOP for closing month-end books"
      → an SOP for month-end close exists                determined
    "build an FAQ page about our returns policy"
      → an FAQ page covering the returns policy exists   determined
    "write an SOP"                    → not established (subject)
    "create a dashboard"              → not established (subject)
    "build an AI financial advisor"   → not established (no test)

  Note: purpose-shaped variation between two instances of the same
  artefact is carried by audience and register, which open
  independently. Objective carries the end state, not the rationale
  for it.
```

The no-new-noun rule is the primary anti-invention safeguard on the highest-leverage slot. It is mechanical and auditable: compare the noun set of the populated value against the noun set of the input.

---

## §3 Rendering of unresolved slots

```
D.11  RENDERING

  none stated        Input addressed nothing here and nothing
                     further is expected. Terminal.
                     Requirement slots only.

  not established    Remains open after discovery.
                     Definition slots only.
                     MUST also appear in open:.

  [N/A] — <reason>   Inapplicable to this goal. Reason required.
                     Any slot.

  open: <slots>      Closing line. Every slot rendered
                     "not established", comma-separated, in
                     contract order. Omitted entirely if none.

  Bounded at four entries by D.8.

D.11a  [N/A] REASONS

  ≤12 words. Single clause. No conjunction. Must name the property
  of the goal that makes the slot inapplicable.

  Over-length is corrected at review, not at render time.

    ✓  [N/A] — fixed at interface design, not goal level
    ✗  [N/A] — form is software; register is fixed at interface
       design, not at goal level          (13 words, two clauses)
```

Rationale, local: uniform tokens across all unresolved slots make every gap look equally consequential, which draws attention away from the gaps that change what gets built. Differentiated forms let a reader distinguish *nothing expected here* from *this must be resolved*, and `open:` collects the latter in one place so it is read rather than scanned. The `[N/A]` cap exists so that reason text does not reacquire the weight the uniform token had.

---

## §4 Type 2 scaffolding

```
G.3a  SCAFFOLDING

  A Type 2 question MAY carry illustrative examples drawn from the
  fixed bank for that slot. Banks are fixed in this spec and are
  NEVER generated, filtered, reordered, or extended per case.

  Examples communicate answer shape, not answer content. They are
  not options, defaults, recommendations, or an exhaustive
  category set. An answer is user-derived whether or not it
  matches an example.

  Bank constraints:
    · 3–5 entries
    · one abstraction level above the expected answer
    · spanning the dimension, not clustered within it
    · at least one entry not domain-adjacent to typical inputs
    · alphabetical order, carrying no ranking

  Render: vertical, one entry per line, bulleted. Entries are
  NEVER numbered, lettered, or otherwise indexed.

  Every bank is followed immediately by the own-words line for
  that slot.

  Round header, once:
    "Anything you skip will be left open rather than guessed."

  Skipping sends the slot to open:. It never populates a value.

G.3b  REPLY HANDLING

  A reply consisting only of an index or ordinal reference to a
  bank entry — "3", "the second one", "the last option" — is not
  an answer. Re-ask once, restating that the entries are examples
  rather than choices. A second such reply sends the slot to open:.

  A reply that matches a bank entry verbatim IS an answer. It is
  populated unannotated. Coincidence between a fixed generic
  entry and a user's actual answer is expected and carries no
  provenance mark.
```

**Sign-off needed on G.3b.** Vertical layout makes entries visually addressable in a way the inline form did not; without this rule a user can select rather than answer and the value that lands is the bank's, not theirs. Non-indexing plus this rule is what preserves the scaffolding/menu distinction structurally, so it survives the layout change without relying on a disclaimer.

### Banks

```
objective — "What should be true when this is done?"
             (Describe the end state, not the thing being built.)

  Examples of the kind of answer:

    • a decision is made
    • a document exists
    • a process runs without you
    • someone's behaviour changes

  Describe it in your own words, or say "skip".


audience — "Who is this for?"
            (Describe the intended audience.)

  Examples of the kind of answer:

    • businesses
    • internal employees
    • retail investors
    • students

  Describe another audience in your own words, or say "skip".


environment — "Where does this operate?"
               (Describe the setting or constraints it runs under.)

  Examples of the kind of answer:

    • a regulated industry
    • a school
    • a team with no technical staff
    • an offline setting
    • an open-source project

  Describe another environment in your own words, or say "skip".


form — "What form should the result take?"

  Examples of the kind of answer:

    • a checklist
    • a conversation
    • a piece of software
    • a training session
    • a written document

  Describe another form in your own words, or say "skip".
```

Known and accepted cost: fixed generic banks will occasionally coincide with the true answer for a given domain — `retail investors` for financial-services inputs. When that happens, discovery and echo are indistinguishable. This is the price of fixing the banks, and it is the correct side of the trade: a generated bank would coincide deliberately and constantly.

---

## §5 Worked example

**Input:** *"I want to build an AI financial advisor. It has to be FCA compliant. I don't want it giving specific product recommendations."*

D.9: environment determined (FCA names a regulatory regime), form determined ("build" + "AI"), exclusions stated. D.9a: objective undetermined — no completion test in "an AI financial advisor", and any end state would import absent nouns (*retirement*, *plan*). Audience undetermined.

```
objective:    not established
audience:     not established
environment:  UK retail financial services (FCA-regulated)
form:         software product
exclusions:   no specific product recommendations
invalidation: none stated
success:      none stated
horizon:      none stated
register:     [N/A] — fixed at interface design, not goal level

open: objective, audience
```

**Type 2 round:**

```
Anything you skip will be left open rather than guessed.

1. What should be true when this is done?
   (Describe the end state, not the thing being built.)

   Examples of the kind of answer:

     • a decision is made
     • a document exists
     • a process runs without you
     • someone's behaviour changes

   Describe it in your own words, or say "skip".

2. Who is this for?
   (Describe the intended audience.)

   Examples of the kind of answer:

     • businesses
     • internal employees
     • retail investors
     • students

   Describe another audience in your own words, or say "skip".
```

**After partial answer** — Q2 answered `retail investors — people with savings but no adviser`, Q1 skipped:

```
objective:    not established
audience:     retail investors — people with savings but no adviser
environment:  UK retail financial services (FCA-regulated)
form:         software product
exclusions:   no specific product recommendations
invalidation: none stated
success:      none stated
horizon:      none stated
register:     [N/A] — fixed at interface design, not goal level

open: objective
```

Audience populated unannotated despite partial overlap with a bank entry (G.3b). Objective remains open. A reader has one unambiguous instruction: the end state is unresolved and must be asked before anything is optimised against it.

---

## §6 Superseded

```
REMOVED   [UNSPECIFIED] token, all uses          → D.11
REMOVED   inline provenance marks [default],
          [assumed], [inferred]                   → D.9 (no
                                                     population
                                                     without
                                                     determination)
REMOVED   adoption-on-silence                     → G.3a
REMOVED   per-case generated examples             → G.3a
REMOVED   selectable option sets                  → G.3a, G.3b
REMOVED   echo-rate threshold (>40%)              → §7
```

Provenance marks are removed rather than softened because they decay: any reader that re-emits rather than passes through drops the mark and keeps the value, so after two hops the annotation is gone and an inferred value is indistinguishable from a stated one. Leaving the slot unpopulated is the only form of the warning that survives re-emission.

---

## §7 Changelog note on the echo threshold

Recorded explicitly so a later reviewer does not read the absence as an oversight:

```
The >40% echo-rate threshold proposed during review was
DELIBERATELY NOT ADOPTED. No owner exists for periodic sampling of
answers against banks, and an unmonitored metric in spec text reads
as a guarantee it does not provide.

Echo is controlled structurally instead:
  · banks fixed in spec, never generated
  · entries generic enough that none is a complete answer
  · entries spanning the dimension
  · ≥1 entry not domain-adjacent
  · entries never indexed (G.3a)
  · index/ordinal replies rejected (G.3b)

If an owner is later identified, the threshold may be reinstated as
a review-time check. It must not be reinstated as spec text without
one.
```

---

